**PASS.** I loaded the current build cold at localhost:8000 and watched it start, and found no loading or startup defect. The report is at `artifacts/logs/reviewer_site.0fZGKo/report.md`.

- **Build identity:** This is the same build as the prior reports: HEAD e500c44 plus uncommitted changes, with the same diff hash (92e25d72…) and `doom.wasm` 7afb94fa…. Nothing in `platform/`, `web/` or the Makefile is newer than `dist/`, and `make -n` has nothing to do, so I didn't rebuild.
- **Server:** Nothing was running on port 8000, so I started a server on `dist/` myself. All 7 files came back 200 with the right content types, and what was served matched `dist/` byte for byte. I stopped only that server afterwards.
- **Cold load:** With the browser cache cleared, the HTML, JS, WASM and data files (the WAD is inside `doom.data`) all loaded with 200. There were no failed requests, no page errors and no console errors. The engine was already running at the first check, 24 ms in, with the title screen fully drawn. The only warnings were 2 from Chrome blocking audio until the user clicks, which is expected.
- **Picture:** The title screen, the demo, the Escape menu and an 800x600 window all look right, with correct colours and no red/blue swap. I checked these by eye from the screenshots.
- **Speed and responsiveness:** The game ran at 34.97 tics/s, against Doom's normal 35. The longest gap between frames was 10.3 ms, so the page was never frozen. The menu opens and closes, and the demo keeps running behind it, as in the original game.
- **Layout:** The game keeps its 16:10 shape at both window sizes, with no scrollbars.

Still open from earlier reports, none of them startup bugs:
- **Coder:** the tab title briefly shows "Doom (WASM)" before the game sets it. This is cosmetic, and I didn't catch it this run.
- **Tester:** the expected results in `tests/faults.sh` need correcting, and the checks need to allow for the ~1.1 s screen-melt pause.
- **Human:** Firefox, Safari, high-DPI screens, and audio by ear are still unchecked.

The pass criteria are the same ones earlier runs proposed; no student has approved them yet. The JSON files in the output folder are summaries I copied from the browser results, not raw dumps. I didn't change any source, test or build files.